  "question": "If $\\int_0^1 f(x)dx=3$, what is $\\int_0^1 f(1-x)dx$?",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Using the property of definite integrals:<br /><br />$\\int_0^a f(x)dx=\\int_0^a f(a-x)dx$.<br /><br />For $a=1$, both integrals are equal.<br /><br />Hence the value is $3$.",
